examples.question_text:
Find the area of this parallelogram in $\text{cm}^{2}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(15,4)--(3,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (3,4)--(3,0);
\draw (3,0.4)--(3.4,0.4)--(3.4,0);
\path (6,0) node[below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (3,2) node[right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.5,2) node[left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The base is $12\text{ cm}$ and its perpendicular height is $4\text{ cm}$. The slanted side is not the height.

Cut along the perpendicular height. Slide triangle T to the opposite end to form a rectangle, with no gaps or overlaps.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5mm,y=2.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(15,4)--(3,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (3,0)--(3,4);
\draw (3,0.5)--(3.5,0.5)--(3.5,0);
\path (2,1.3) node {$\mathrm{T}$};
\path (6,0) node[below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (3,2.8) node[right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw[->] (16,2)--(18,2);
\begin{scope}[xshift=47.5mm]
\draw (3,0)--(15,0)--(15,4)--(3,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (12,0)--(15,4);
\draw (3,0.5)--(3.5,0.5)--(3.5,0);
\path (14,1.3) node {$\mathrm{T}$};
\path (9,0) node[below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (15,2) node[right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Rearranging the pieces preserves area. The rectangle measures $12\text{ cm}$ by $4\text{ cm}$, so the parallelogram has the same area.

$\begin{align*} A&=bh\\ &=12\times4\\ &=48\text{ cm}^{2}\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
Find the area of this parallelogram in $\text{m}^{2}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (0,0)--(9,0)--(12,4)--(3,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (9,0)--(12,0)--(12,4);
\draw (11.6,0)--(11.6,0.4)--(12,0.4);
\path (4.5,0) node[below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\path (12,2) node[right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\path (1.5,2) node[left] {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the left-hand side as the base. Find the area of this parallelogram in $\text{cm}^{2}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (0,0)--(0,6)--(4,9)--(4,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,4.5)--(4,4.5);
\draw (0,4.1)--(0.4,4.1)--(0.4,4.5);
\path (0,3) node[left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,4.5) node[above] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,1.5) node[below right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
